this September Volkswagen is planning an  initial public offering for luxury  sports car maker Porsche the IPO is  targeting a 75 billion valuation for  Porsche which would make it Germany's  second largest IPO in history Volkswagen  is expected to price preferred shares of  Porsche AG between 76 Euros 50 cents and  82 Euros 50 cents per share if the upper  range of the proposed price is achieved  it would make Porsche's IPO the third  largest on record in Europe as part of  the listing Porsche's Shares are being  split in two with 455.5 million ordinary  shares and 455.5 million preferred  shares or 911 million shares overall a  number of car enthusiasts will instantly  recognize as Porsche's most iconic model  as part of the deal VW plans to sell 25  plus one ordinary share in Porsche AG to  Porsche SE the holding firm controlled  by the founding Porsche piak family this  will allow the family to retain a  minority stake in the company and have a  say in future company decisions  the Porsche PX family has also agreed to  pay a 7.5 premium on top of the price  range for the preferred shares  other parties with planned stakes in  Porsche include the Sovereign wealth  funds of Qatar Abu Dhabi and Norway as  well as the mutual fund company T Rowe  Price  with the expected 9.4 billion dollars it  raises from the IPO Volkswagen will  finance a shift to electric vehicles and  future investments in software  development  Porsche Shares are expected to begin  trading on the Frankfurt Stock Exchange  on September 29th  foreign
 

